INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(44000, 0, 440, 0, 0, 0, 'Tanaris', 'Tanaris is a sea of shifting sand in the far southeast of Kalimdor, south of Thousand Needles and east of Un''Goro Crater. Trolls ruled this land long ago, and the ruins of their old sites still lie half buried among the dunes. Sand trolls of the Sandfury tribe still hold the walled city of Zul''Farrak in the northwest. The goblins of the Steamwheedle Cartel have made the rest of the desert their business. Their town of Gadgetzan lives on water drawn from beneath the dunes, yet the Wastewander nomads have seized most of its wells, and Southsea pirates prey on the cartel''s ships from a cove on the eastern coast. Older and stranger powers lie deeper in. Silithid hives drain the desert pools, Dunemaul ogres camp among the troll ruins, and in the south great giants walk before the sealed gates of Uldum. In the eastern mountains the bronze dragonflight keeps the Caverns of Time, where the paths of history meet.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tanaris (jungle in the Gurubashi empire, Sundering, Farraki become sand trolls, Steamwheedle Cartel centers, bronze flight at the Caverns of Time, Uldum entrance); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Zul''Farrak (Sandfury city in northwestern Tanaris); quest 1690 description (Wastewander have seized almost all the water wells); quests 8366, 2875 (Southsea pirates at Lost Rigger Cove); quests 992, 82 (silithid drain the water pools); quest 5863 description (Dunemaul ogres, old troll ruins); DB: Dune Smasher 5469 (giant, type 5) spawned in areas 989 and 990; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tanaris (jungle claim rests on a 2018 designer tweet; Farraki naming is later lore: both removed); quest 3161 (trolls used to occupy this land); quest 2873 (walled pirate town)'),
(44001, 1, 440, 1, 0, 0, 'Gadgetzan', 'Gadgetzan is the chief town of the Steamwheedle Cartel in Kalimdor, a walled goblin settlement among the dunes of northern Tanaris. Like every cartel town it is neutral ground. Anyone with coin is welcome, and the town''s bruisers fall hard on whoever starts trouble, asking only whether the culprit really meant to make them hurt someone. Water is the town''s lifeblood and its biggest business, managed by the Gadgetzan Water Company, whose officials fret over every well the nomads steal. Around them work alchemists, smiths, engineers and inventors, and the innkeeper sizes up newcomers for the cage matches fought in the town''s arena. Flight masters for both the Alliance and the Horde keep their mounts here.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Gadgetzan (capital of the Steamwheedle Cartel, neutral, bruisers attack those who fight, water as liquid gold, Thunderdrome arena); creature_text 9460 (Gadgetzan Bruiser lines); npc_text 3566 (Innkeeper Fizzgrimble: cage matches); quests 1690, 992 (Gadgetzan Water Company and the nomads); DB area 976: Bera Stonehammer 7823 (faction 12), Bulkrek Ragefist 7824 (faction 29), Trenton Lighthammer, Krinkle Goodsteel, Nixx Sprocketspring, Alchemist Pestlezugg'),
(44002, 1, 440, 2, 0, 0, 'Steamwheedle Port', 'Steamwheedle Port is the cartel''s harbor on the northeastern coast of Tanaris, linked by road to Gadgetzan, where ships run to and from Booty Bay. Security Chief Bilgewhizzle keeps the peace on its docks. Stoley tends bar and swears by his Steamwheedle bilge rum, thick as gravel and fiery as lava. A haughty fashion designer procures the latest styles for queens and warchiefs, a troll mystic named Yeh''kinya pursues his studies along the shore, and the gnome soothsayer Narain Soothfancy keeps house just to the north. South of the port waits Torta, a turtle whose husband Tooga went out to fetch dinner and has not found his way home.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Steamwheedle_Port (east coast port, road to Gadgetzan, residents); quest 2876 (shipments between Steamwheedle Port and Booty Bay); quests 2872, 2874 (Stoley, bilge rum thick as gravel, burns like lava); quest 8365 (Haughty Modiste: Kings and Queens, Warchiefs); quests 3520, 5065 (Yeh''kinya, Ironboot at the port); DB: Narain Soothfancy 11811 at map 65,19, north of the port; quest 1560 description and creature_text 5955, 6015 (Torta south of the port)'),
(44003, 1, 440, 3, 0, 0, 'Noonshade Ruins', 'On the road between Gadgetzan and Steamwheedle Port lie the Noonshade Ruins, a scatter of ancient troll stonework half buried in the sand. Whoever raised them is long gone. The ruins now shelter Wastewander thieves and bandits, who lie in wait among the stones, and starving blisterpaw hyenas and scorpid hunters prowl the dunes around them. Purple lotus grows among the broken walls for those bold enough to pick it.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Noonshade_Ruins (ancient troll ruins east of Gadgetzan, Wastewander overran them); DB area 1937: Wastewander Thief x7, Wastewander Bandit x4, Starving Blisterpaw, Scorpid Hunter, Purple Lotus x10; centroid of area 1937 spawns at map 60,24, between Gadgetzan (52,28) and the port (67,22)'),
(44004, 1, 440, 4, 0, 0, 'Waterspring Field', 'Waterspring Field, east of Gadgetzan, is the reason the town can survive at all. The goblins raised water towers here to pump the hidden reserves beneath the desert. The Wastewander nomads took the field for themselves, and their rogues, shadow mages and assassins now guard the towers and the wells the Gadgetzan Water Company counts as its own. Their leader, Caliph Scorpidsting, is found here among them, and the Water Company has posted a price on his head for murdering its workers and seizing its property.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Waterspring_Field (water towers pump underground reserves; Wastewanders hijacked them); quests 1690, 1691 (nomads seized the wells, east of Gadgetzan); quest 1707 (water pouches are our water anyway); quest 2781 (Caliph Scorpidsting: murder, theft, seizing property); DB area 985: Wastewander Shadow Mage, Rogue, Thief, Assassin, Bandit; Caliph Scorpidsting 7847'),
(44005, 1, 440, 5, 0, 0, 'Lost Rigger Cove', 'Ringed by mountains south of Steamwheedle Port lies Lost Rigger Cove, the hideout of the Southsea pirates. Their walled town has docks and a shipyard, and cargo taken from cartel ships lies about it, including the rum shipment Captain Cuergo stole from Stoley. The cartel pays the pirates protection money, yet lately they ignore the bargain. The pirate Andre Firebeard is wanted for crimes against Steamwheedle and Gadgetzan, and a goblin cutthroat named Kregg Keelhaul is sometimes seen in the cove. A treasure map even claims Cuergo buried a chest of gold on a beach further south.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Lost_Rigger_Cove (Southsea hideout, mountains on three sides, shipyard); quest 2873 (Cuergo stole the rum, walled pirate town to the south); quest 8366 (protection money disregarded); quest 2875 (Andre Firebeard wanted); quest 2882 (Cuergo''s Gold map: south of Wheedle); DB area 1336: Southsea Pirate, Freebooter, Dock Worker, Swashbuckler; Andre Firebeard 7883; Kregg Keelhaul 8203; Stolen Cargo objects; benches and chairs; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Kregg_Keelhaul (rare goblin, Southsea Freebooters)'),
(44006, 1, 440, 6, 0, 0, 'Southbreak Shore', 'South of Lost Rigger Cove the coast opens into Southbreak Shore, a long flat beach washed by the South Seas. Surf gliders, great sea turtles, haul themselves through the shallows, and the beach belongs to giants: coast striders wade along the tide line and a deep dweller lurks in the water beyond. Few travelers linger. On a small island just offshore lives a gnome named Winkey, keeping his own company.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Southbreak_Shore (flat beach south of Lost Rigger Cove, sea giants and turtles once roamed, Winkey on an island); DB area 1940: Surf Glider 5431 (family 21, turtle) x39, Coast Strider 5466 x10 and Deep Dweller 5467 (type 5 giants), Winkey 7770'),
(44007, 1, 440, 7, 0, 0, 'Caverns of Time', 'In the mountains of eastern Tanaris a great cavern opens into the realm of Nozdormu, the Timeless One. Here the bronze dragonflight has watched over the flow of time since the world was young, and its guardians bar any who would meddle with it. Before the entrance stands Anachronos, heir of Nozdormu, in his true dragon form, and nearby wait his far less welcoming dragonkin companions Tick, Chronalis and Occulus, who suffer no mortal to come near.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Caverns_of_Time (bronze flight guards since the world was young, Nozdormu''s home, Anachronos outside with Tick, Chronalis, Occulus); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Anachronos (heir of Nozdormu); npc_text 9977 (Steward of Time: beyond this hall lies dangers); quest 10279 (a brother flies you to the master''s lair); broadcast_text 17657, 17661 (Timeless One, timeways); DB area 2300: Anachronos 15192, Steward of Time 20142, Tick 8198, Chronalis 8197, Occulus 8196'),
(44008, 1, 440, 8, 0, 0, 'Broken Pillar', 'South of Gadgetzan a few toppled columns mark the Broken Pillar, the remains of a troll site lost to the sands. Its newest resident is Marvon Rivetseeker, a goblin scholar from Ratchet who crashed his zeppelin nearby and decided to begin his research where he landed. From his camp he studies the troll ruins of the desert and the ornaments of Gahz''ridian the old trolls carved in honor of the hydra Gahz''rilla, and he speaks of what he once saw within the Sunken Temple.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Broken_Pillar (troll ruins south of Gadgetzan; Marvon''s camp); npc_text 2038 (home in Ratchet, crashed zeppelin, started research here); quest 3161 (Gahz''ridian ornaments modeled on Gahz''rilla); quests 3380, 3445 (studies the troll ruins in Tanaris), 3444 (Sunken Temple); DB: Marvon Rivetseeker 7771 in area 1938 at map 53,46'),
(44009, 1, 440, 9, 0, 0, 'Abyssal Sands', 'The Abyssal Sands are the empty heart of Tanaris, a rolling waste of dunes between Gadgetzan and the southern ruins. Little shade and less water can be found here. Fire rocs and their larger kin circle overhead, glasshide basilisks bask on the dunes, and packs of blisterpaw hyenas and scorpids roam the sand in search of prey. Whirling vortexes of wind drift across the waste, and travelers speak of a great firebird that is sometimes seen soaring above it.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Abyssal_Sands (endless dune sea); DB area 1939: Fire Roc x31, Roc x9, Glasshide Gazer and Basilisk, Blisterpaw Hyena x39, Scorpid Dunestalker and Tail Lasher, Gusting Vortex 8667 x3, Greater Firebird 8207 (rare, family 7); centroid of area 1939 at map 46,40'),
(44010, 1, 440, 10, 0, 0, 'Sandsorrow Watch', 'West of Gadgetzan, Sandfury trolls guard Sandsorrow Watch, an outpost of watch towers standing over a pool of open water, a rare treasure in the desert. Firecallers, hideskinners and axe throwers patrol its sands, and they do not welcome goblin surveyors. The Gadgetzan Water Company covets the pool all the same and sends its junior surveyors to sample it in plain sight of the trolls. A troll called Jin''Zallah the Sandbringer is said to walk among them.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Sandsorrow_Watch (west of Gadgetzan, held by Sandfury trolls, watch tower, protecting what little water exists); quest 992 description and reward text (pool near Sandsorrow Watch, in sight of the trolls; ambushed by a creepy-crawly); DB area 979: Sandfury Firecaller x20, Axe Thrower x10, Hideskinner x6, Jin''Zallah the Sandbringer 8200 (rank 2); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Jin''Zallah_the_Sandbringer (rare Sandfury sand troll)'),
(44011, 1, 440, 11, 0, 0, 'Zul''Farrak', 'In the northwest of Tanaris rise the walls of Zul''Farrak, city of the Sandfury trolls, ruthless sand trolls steeped in dark magic who attack anyone who approaches. Warleader Krazzilak prowls before its gates. Legends cling to the place. A hydra god, Gahz''rilla, is said to dwell in a sacred pool within its walls, and the persecutors of the martyr Theka are said to scuttle about his shrine, cursed into scarabs. Many are drawn inside all the same: Sergeant Bly led his band in hunting treasure, the Prophecy of Mosh''aru lies on tablets within, and the smith Trenton Lighthammer of Gadgetzan still remembers with dread the warband that once marched out of it to lay waste to the land.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Zul''Farrak (Sandfury, ruthlessness and dark mysticism, attack anyone who approaches, Gahz''rilla in a sacred pool); quest 3527 (tablets held by Theka and Velratha, persecutors cursed into scarabs); quest 2768 (Sergeant Bly treasure hunting in Zul''Farrak); npc_text 1758 (Trenton Lighthammer: a warband from Zul''Farrak laid waste to the land); DB area 978: Warleader Krazzilak 8199 (rank 2), Sandfury Firecaller, Hideskinner, Axe Thrower, meeting stone'),
(44012, 1, 440, 12, 0, 0, 'The Noxious Lair', 'On the western edge of Tanaris, above the jungles of Un''Goro Crater, the ground sinks into a broad hollow where pools of water once gathered. They are gone now, drained by the Centipaar silithid who have dug their hive into the sand. Their workers, tunnelers and stingers swarm over the hollow, their eggs lie clustered in the earth, and their sandreavers guard the hive mounds. The Gadgetzan Water Company wants to know what these bugs are, and seeks parts of them for Alchemist Pestlezugg to study. A great devourer named Soriid is said to hunt among the hives.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Noxious_Lair (Centipaar hive, there used to be water, sunken surface, overlooks Un''Goro); quest 82 description (bugs draining the water pools where the Noxious Lair is); quests 82, 110 reward texts (Pestlezugg''s analysis); DB area 982: Centipaar Stinger, Wasp, Swarmer, Worker, Tunneler, Sandreaver; Silithid Egg x24; Soriid the Devourer 8204 (rare, silithid)'),
(44013, 1, 440, 13, 0, 0, 'Dunemaul Compound', 'Not long ago a large band of nomadic Dunemaul ogres wandered into Tanaris and claimed a stretch of desert south of Gadgetzan, building a compound there. Brutes and enforcers guard it, warlocks and ogre mages practice their crude magic, and smaller bands have spread out to occupy the old troll ruins nearby. In Gadgetzan, Andi Lynn fears the force the ogres could build and wants the compound broken before it grows, beginning with its leader, Gor''marok the Ravager. Two rarely seen ogres, Cyclok the Mad and Omgorn the Lost, prowl the camp as well.', 'quest 5863 description (nomadic ogres recently arrived, compound south of Gadgetzan, smaller bands invaded the old troll ruins, Gor''marok the Ravager); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dunemaul_Compound (ogre mound of the Dunemaul clan; Gor''marok former leader); DB area 983: Dunemaul Brute x24, Enforcer x18, Warlock x6, Ogre Mage x3, Gor''marok 12046, Cyclok the Mad 8202, Omgorn the Lost 8201 (both rare); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Omgorn_the_Lost (rare Dunemaul ogre, a spawn at each ogre camp)'),
(44014, 1, 440, 14, 0, 0, 'Eastmoon Ruins', 'West of the Gaping Chasm lie the Eastmoon Ruins, ancient troll stonework slowly swallowed by the dunes. The Dunemaul ogres have spread here from their compound, and their warlocks and ogre mages have made the ruins a camp of their own. Glasshide basilisks and blisterpaw hyenas haunt the edges, purple lotus grows in the shelter of the old walls, and the rarely seen ogre wanderer Omgorn the Lost passes through.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Eastmoon_Ruins (ancient troll ruins just west of the Gaping Chasm; Dunemaul ogres took the area); quest 5863 (smaller ogre bands invaded the old troll ruins); DB area 984: Dunemaul Warlock x7, Ogre Mage x3, Enforcer, Brute; Glasshide Gazer; Blisterpaw; Purple Lotus x6; Omgorn the Lost 8201'),
(44015, 1, 440, 15, 0, 0, 'Southmoon Ruins', 'North of the Valley of the Watchers stand the Southmoon Ruins, another troll site from the days when trolls held this land. Dunemaul ogres camp among the fallen stones. The ground here is rich in Gahz''ridian, the strange element the old trolls carved into ornaments in honor of their hydra god, and a goblin treasure hunter at the Broken Pillar rewards those who bring him pieces. Searing rocs circle overhead.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Southmoon_Ruins (ancient troll ruins north of the Valley of the Watchers, Dunemaul once controlled them); quest 3161 (Gahz''ridian ornaments, trolls who used to occupy this land); DB area 992: Gahz''ridian objects x23, Dunemaul Ogre, Enforcer, Brute, Warlock; Searing Roc x7'),
(44016, 1, 440, 16, 0, 0, 'The Gaping Chasm', 'Southeast of Gadgetzan the desert splits open into the Gaping Chasm, now a hive of the Hazzali silithid. Wasps, swarmers and stingers boil out of its great mounds, while workers and tunnelers dig ever deeper below. Junior Surveyor Scrimshank of the Gadgetzan Water Company was sent here, and his last report spoke of the same strange bugs before he went missing. A ravenous silithid called Haarka is feared in the depths, and near the chasm lies a crashed gnomish homing robot, OOX-17/TN, waiting for someone to come to its rescue.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/The_Gaping_Chasm (silithid hive in southeastern Tanaris, Hazzali, Scrimshank went missing and died); quest 10 description and reward text (Scrimshank, Gaping Chasm); quest 351 description (OOX-17/TN crashed near the Gaping Chasm); DB area 981: Hazzali Wasp, Swarmer, Worker, Stinger, Tunneler, Sandreaver; Scrimshank''s Surveying Gear 144053; Haarka the Ravenous 8205 (rare, silithid); DB: Homing Robot OOX-17/TN 7784 spawned at -8851,-4374 near the chasm'),
(44017, 1, 440, 17, 0, 0, 'Thistleshrub Valley', 'In the southwestern corner of Tanaris lies Thistleshrub Valley, a low basin where great cacti grow thick in the heat. Its guardians are living plants: gnarled thistleshrubs and rootshapers that lash out at anything that comes near, and dew collectors that store precious water in special glands. That water has drawn more than one schemer from Gadgetzan. Marin Noggenfogger sought the glands for a drink to quench his thirst, and Tran''rek of Gadgetzan wants a closer look at the valley''s cactus, if only someone else will clear the way first.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thistleshrub_Valley (southwestern edge, one of the lowest spots, massive cacti, elementals of living vines attack, RPG section); quest 2605 (dew collectors store water in glands, cactus garden to the southwest); quest 3362 description and completion text (gnarled thistleshrubs and rootshapers, Tran''rek wants a closer look at the cactus); DB area 980: Thistleshrub Dew Collector x14, Rootshaper x11, Gnarled Thistleshrub x8 (type 4 elementals)'),
(44018, 1, 440, 18, 0, 0, 'Valley of the Watchers', 'In the far southwest of Tanaris a valley runs between the mountains to a great sealed gate, the entrance to Uldum. Few believe the place behind it is more than a myth. The gate cannot be forced, and huge giants, the Dune Smashers, walk the valley floor as if keeping watch over it. Before the gate stands a stone pedestal, silent to those who pass it by. Prospector Gunstan of the Explorers'' League keeps a lonely camp in the valley, among the few who come here at all.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Valley_of_the_Watchers (southern Tanaris, impenetrable gate into Uldum, Dune Smashers lived here); quest 2954 (Stone Watcher of Norgannon at the Uldum Pedestal, Plates of Uldum); ironforge.json 153714 and thunder_bluff.json 163817 (the disc chains; told there); DB areas 989 and 990: Dune Smasher 5469 x6 (giant), Uldum Pedestal 142343, Prospector Gunstan 5389 (Explorers'' League)'),
(44019, 1, 440, 19, 0, 0, 'Land''s End Beach', 'Land''s End Beach is the southernmost shore of Tanaris, in the far southeast of Kalimdor, where the desert finally runs out into the South Seas. Surf gliders by the dozen crawl through the breakers. A mermaid named Meridith dwells in the waters here, and she still treasures the day she pulled a gnome from the wreck of his flying machine on this very beach. That gnome was Narain Soothfancy, who had hidden a precious book on a small island further south and crashed on the way home. A pirate''s treasure map claims that Captain Cuergo buried his gold on this shore, by a mast, a flag and bones.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Land''s_End_Beach (southernmost point of Tanaris, far southeast of Kalimdor, islands offshore); quest 8599 description (Meridith rescued the gnome from the crashed flying machine); quest 8597 description (crashed gyrocopter on Land''s End Beach, book hidden on an island to the south); npc_text 7917 (Meridith: ocean floor is peaceful); DB area 987: Surf Glider x95, Meridith the Mermaiden 15526, Inconspicuous Landmark 142189 x6 (for quest 2882 Cuergo''s Gold)'),
(44020, 2, 440, 1, 0, 0, 'Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser', 'Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser of the Gadgetzan Water Company has one great worry: with the nomads holding the wells, the town must find its water somewhere else. His answer is to survey the desert for fresh sources, and he will sign on almost any likely stranger as a temporary junior-grade surveyor, hand over a dowsing widget and send them off to sample far-flung pools, even those within sight of the Sandfury trolls. He leans on his top assistant, Junior Surveyor Scrimshank, and counts the alchemist Pestlezugg an old friend.', 'quest 992 description and reward text; quest 10 description and reward text (top assistant, a good goblin); quest 113 reward text (not thrilled about handing out information; known Pestlezugg for years); creature_template 7724 subname Gadgetzan Water Co., faction 475'),
(44021, 2, 440, 2, 0, 0, 'Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle', 'Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle of the Gadgetzan Water Company is as fierce about profit as he is about justice for the Wastewander nomads who stole his wells. He rewards those who thin the nomads'' ranks, pays the company''s bounty on their leader Caliph Scorpidsting, and sells off the model 4711-FTZ power sources that once ran the wells, now in surplus thanks to the thieves, reminding buyers that nothing is free in Gadgetzan. He dreams aloud of importing water from the icy springs of Dun Morogh. He also wants back his cherished divino-matic rod, the tool he uses to find new water holes, stolen by a mercenary named Sergeant Bly who led his band into Zul''Farrak.', 'quests 1690, 1691, 2781 (bounties); quest 243 reward text (4711-FTZ power sources, over abundance because of the nomads, nothing''s free in Gadgetzan); quest 654 completion text (import water from the icy springs of Dun Morogh); quest 2768 description (divino-matic rod, Sergeant Bly, Zul''Farrak); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Zul''Farrak (Bly''s band of mercenaries)'),
(44022, 2, 440, 3, 0, 0, 'Marin Noggenfogger', 'Marin Noggenfogger is a Gadgetzan goblin with a terrible thirst and a nose for profit. Living out in the desert is rough, he complains, and standing about in the heat leaves him parched. Lately he has set his hopes on the dew collectors of Thistleshrub Valley, living plants said to hoard water in glands of their own. A drink brewed from one of those, he reckons, would put an end to his thirst for good.', 'npc_text 1493 (so thirsty standing outside in this heat); quests 2605, 2606 (Sprinkle an excellent chef; a little eccentric); quests 2641, 2661, 2662 (Violet Powder; millions; such a kidder); creature_text 7564'),
(44023, 2, 440, 4, 0, 0, 'Curgle Cranklehop', 'Curgle Cranklehop is a Gadgetzan inventor with a soft spot for birds. He is helping the druids save the hippogryphs of Feralas, whose numbers are dwindling under the blight of the Gordunni ogres, and to that end he built the Super Egg-O-Matic, a machine that weighs, measures and packs any hippogryph egg brought to it. He collects eggs of every quality, grieving gently over the ones that cannot be saved, and sends crates of them to Erelas Ambersky in Rut''theran Village to hatch. His latest invention, the Super Snapper FX, takes pictures of anything it is aimed at.', 'npc_text 1519 (Super Egg-O-Matic, aiding the druids to save the hippogryphs, Gordunni); quests 2741 reward text (weighed, measured and packaged), 2747, 2750; quest 3022 (crate to Erelas Ambersky in Rut''theran); quest 2944 description (Super Snapper FX); feralas.json 35735 (the Stave of Equinex chain uses the camera; not retold)'),
(44024, 2, 440, 5, 0, 0, 'Marvon Rivetseeker', 'Marvon Rivetseeker is a goblin scientist from Ratchet and a treasure hunter at heart. He came to Tanaris by zeppelin to study its troll ruins, crashed, and simply began his research where he landed, at the Broken Pillar. He collects the Gahz''ridian ornaments the old trolls carved after the hydra Gahz''rilla, finding them with a detector helmet of his own invention. He once entered the Sunken Temple and barely escaped through its ooze-flooded halls, and all he remembers of it is a large circular room filled with serpent statues. He has sent for a round stone bearing the same serpent symbol, hoping it will tell him more.', 'npc_text 2038; quest 3161 (scientist, treasure hunter, Gahz''ridian, detector); quests 3444, 3446, 3447 (Sunken Temple memories); quests 3380, 3445 (left his home in Ratchet to study the troll ruins in Tanaris); quests 3446, 3447 (circle of statues holds the secret to a greater treasure)'),
(44025, 2, 440, 6, 0, 0, 'Yeh''kinya', 'Yeh''kinya is an old troll mystic living at Steamwheedle Port. Time and drink, he admits, have dulled his outer senses, though his inner eyes remain strong. His studies turn on an ancient god whom he will not yet name, and he believes the screechers of the Feralas vales are kin to that god, their spirits bound to him still. He wants someone to go and gather their essence, and to whoever does, he promises to reveal more about the god.', 'npc_text 2140 (time and drink have dulled my outer senses); quest 3520 reward text; quests 3527, 4787, 3528; quest 8181 reward text and creature_text 8579 (Blood and souls for Hakkar); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Yeh''kinya (troll at Steamwheedle Port, worships Hakkar)'),
(44026, 2, 440, 7, 0, 0, 'Prospector Ironboot', 'Prospector Ironboot is an old dwarf scholar who works among the goblins of Steamwheedle Port, far from the halls of his own people. He has studied the troll legends of Hakkar the Soulflayer for a long time, above all the prophecy of Mosh''aru, which the trolls set down upon tablets, and he fears that what those tablets hold will prove a great threat to the world.', 'quests 5065, 4788, 8181, 8182 descriptions and reward texts; quest 8181 reward text (that old dwarf Ironboot, meddling prospector); DB: Prospector Ironboot 10460 in area 977'),
(44027, 2, 440, 8, 0, 0, 'Narain Soothfancy', 'Narain Soothfancy is a gnome who lives just north of Steamwheedle Port and calls himself a psychic, though his guesses rarely land: he will press an unopened envelope to his forehead and announce what lies inside, usually wrongly. A copy of Soothsaying for Dummies sits by his door. He claims a crash on Land''s End Beach gave him his super-gnomish powers, and he nurses a long list of grudges, chief among them his arch-enemy, Doctor Weavil.', 'npc_text 7902 (envelope guess; Soothsaying for Dummies book); quest 8597 (crash gave him super-gnomish psychic powers); quests 8577, 8620 (Stewvul, Doctor Weavil); quest 8599 reward text (She''s a fish); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Narain_Soothfancy (lived north of Steamwheedle Port; Azuregos: terrible psychic, amazing engineer); gameobject 177226 Book Soothsaying for Dummies in area 977; npc_text 7897 (Azuregos: terrible, terrible psychic but an amazing engineer)'),
(44028, 2, 440, 9, 0, 0, 'Anachronos', 'Anachronos, heir of Nozdormu the Timeless One, keeps watch before the Caverns of Time in his true dragon form, a great bronze dragon watching over the approach to his master''s realm, his dragonkin companions never far away. He has few words for the mortals who pass, and those few are grim. He speaks as though a war were close at hand: this time, he insists, the first strike must be theirs, so that the mistakes of the past are not repeated. To passing visitors he does not say what those mistakes were.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Anachronos (heir of Nozdormu; qiraji attacked the Caverns; sealed with Fandral; made the scepter; Fandral shattered it after Valstann''s death; shards to Vaelastrasz, Azuregos, Eranikus); quest 8519 reward text (gathered the shards, charge of the Dragonflights); quest 8555 reward text (distrust towards your kind); npc_text 7742 (we must make the first strike; mistakes of the past); quest 8742 (a thousand years has passed)'),
(44029, 2, 440, 10, 0, 0, 'Andormu', 'Andormu is a bronze dragon of the Keepers of Time who wears the shape of an elf, at times a grown man and at times a child, both sometimes seen at once. With his sister Nozari he leads the keepers in the Caverns of Time while Nozdormu is away. Small meddlers hardly concern him, such as a greedy wizard nudging the past to better his station. What troubles him now is worse: strange beings seen more and more often across the timeways, trying to alter the course of history itself. The keepers dare not risk themselves, so Andormu welcomes heroes from Azeroth to defend the timeways in their place.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Andormu (bronze dragon, elf visage, adult and child forms at the same time, sister Nozari, co-leader of the Keepers of Time); creature_text 19932 and 19933 (Andormu and Nozari: greedy wizard, beings tampering with the timeways, master away, heroes due to arrive); quest 10277; creature_text 19932 groups 1 and 2 (greedy wizard improving his station)'),
(44030, 3, 440, 1, 0, 0, 'Bugs in the Water', 'With the Wastewander nomads holding its wells, the Gadgetzan Water Company has gone looking for new water. There is water to be had in the desert, Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser insists, for those smart enough to survey it first, and he has taken on temporary junior surveyors to find it. The first assignment is a pool beside Sandsorrow Watch, in plain sight of the Sandfury trolls: tap a sample with a dowsing widget and bring it back. It sounds simple enough, and the company badly needs it to be, for without the wells the town''s water supply will soon run dry.', 'quests 992, 82, 10, 110, 113 descriptions and reward texts; quests 32 and 162 reward texts (silithid named by Zilzibin Drumlore and Gracina Spiritmight)'),
(44031, 3, 440, 2, 0, 0, 'Wastewander Justice', 'The Wastewander nomads have seized almost every well in Tanaris, and without them Gadgetzan''s water will soon run dry. Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle of the Gadgetzan Water Company calls it a matter of justice, goblin style, and his first order is to thin the nomads'' ranks, starting with the bandits and thieves east of town. Meanwhile Spigot Operator Luglunket pays a company care package for every handful of water pouches taken from the nomads, since that water was the company''s to begin with. Wanted posters in Gadgetzan and Steamwheedle Port name the nomads'' leader, Caliph Scorpidsting, for murdering company workers and stealing its resources and property.', 'quests 1690, 1691 descriptions and reward texts; quest 1707 description and reward text; quest 2781 description and reward text; gameobject_queststarter 142122, 150075 (Wanted Posters in areas 977 and 976) for 2781'),
(44032, 3, 440, 3, 0, 0, 'The Noggenfogger Elixir', 'Marin Noggenfogger of Gadgetzan is thirsty, as anyone who stands about in the Tanaris heat must be. He has heard of strange creatures to the southwest, the dew collectors of Thistleshrub Valley, which store water in special glands, and he is sure that a drink made from one would quench his thirst. All he needs is someone willing to go out to the cactus garden where the dew collectors live and bring a laden gland back to him, so that he can taste it for himself.', 'quests 2605, 2606, 2641, 2661, 2662 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 7564 (mixing the elixir)'),
(44033, 3, 440, 4, 0, 0, 'The Southsea Shakedown', 'The Steamwheedle Cartel pays the Southsea pirates of Lost Rigger Cove to leave its ships alone, but lately the pirates have taken the money and kept raiding. The cartel has leaned on Security Chief Bilgewhizzle of Steamwheedle Port to teach them a lesson, and since he cannot leave the docks he deputizes whoever will go. A wanted decree authorizes lethal force against the pirate Andre Firebeard, adding that his head may stand in for him at his hearing. The port has its own grievances. Captain Cuergo stole Stoley''s last shipment of rum just when Stoley needed it to settle a bet with Sea Wolf MacKinley of Booty Bay, and the Haughty Modiste wants Southsea hats by the score for the elite of Azerothian society.', 'quest 8366 description (protection money, deputize); quest 2875 description (lethal force, head as proxy); quest 2876 description and reward text; quests 2872, 2873 descriptions; quest 8365 description and reward text'),
(44034, 3, 440, 5, 0, 0, 'The Egg of Hakkar', 'The troll mystic Yeh''kinya of Steamwheedle Port seeks the spirits of the vale screechers of Feralas, cousins, he says, of an old, old god whose spirits are still linked to him. He hands out a bramble wand for the task: strike down a screecher, wave the bramble over its body to coax its spirit out, and touch the spirit to gather its essence. Bring back the bramble and the essence, Yeh''kinya promises, and he will tell more of the old god of which he spoke.', 'quests 3520, 3527, 4787, 3528 descriptions and reward texts'),
(44035, 3, 440, 6, 0, 0, 'The Lost Tablets of Mosh''aru', 'After the egg of Hakkar passed into Yeh''kinya''s hands, the dwarf Prospector Ironboot of Steamwheedle Port came forward with a warning: the troll had not told the truth. The two tablets brought to him spoke of containing Hakkar''s essence, but there was more to the legend. Ironboot had found that there are six tablets of Mosh''aru, not two, and he feared what the others would reveal. The third and fourth, he said, are held by the Mossflayer trolls of the Eastern Plaguelands.', 'quests 5065, 4788, 8181, 8182 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 8579'),
(44036, 3, 440, 7, 0, 0, 'The Arcanite Buoy', 'When a hero brought Narain Soothfancy a ledger from the blue dragon Azuregos, the gnome learned that the dragon wanted an arcanite buoy built, and that its plans were written in Draconic, a tongue Narain cannot read. That old goat knows it, he grumbled. Before he could begin he needed three things, not necessarily in that order: his scrying goggles, a five hundred pound chicken, and volume two of Draconic for Dummies. For the chicken he sent his helper to Dirge Quikcleave, the cook of Gadgetzan. The book, he said, was stowed where no one could ever find it, on an island south of Land''s End Beach.', 'quest 8575 reward text, 8576 reward text; quests 8577, 8578; quests 8584, 8585, 8586, 8587; quests 8597, 8598, 8606, 8620; quests 8728, 8729 descriptions; feralas.json note: Isle of Dread chimaerok chains left to Tanaris/Silithus; quest_template 8576 QuestType 0 (autocomplete); QuestHandler.cpp: autocomplete quests go straight to the reward window, no AddQuest'),
(44037, 3, 440, 8, 0, 8, 'The Keepers of Time', 'In the mountains of eastern Tanaris, the threshold of the Caverns of Time is kept by the Steward of Time, one of the Keepers of Time who serve Nozdormu. He meets each traveler as though the visit had long been foreseen, and he does not hide the danger: beyond his hall, he warns, lie perils unheard of in the mortal world. For those willing to go on he offers a swift descent, one of his brothers flying them down to the master''s lair far below, where Andormu of the Keepers of Time awaits the heroes the keepers have been expecting.', 'quests 10279, 10277 descriptions and reward texts; broadcast_text 17656-17667 (Custodian of Time tour); npc_text 9977, 9978 (Steward of Time)');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(44002, 1, 3, 255, 'The port has gained another scholar. Along the shore near Yeh''kinya, the old dwarf Prospector Ironboot keeps a camp of his own among the goblins, a patient student of the troll legends of Hakkar and of the prophecies the trolls once set down on tablets.', 'quest 5065 description (I have studied long; the Mosh''aru tablets); DB: Prospector Ironboot 10460 in area 977; mod-individual-progression ipp_aware_npcs.sql: 10460 scripted npc_ipp_zg, visible from RequiredZulGurubProgression (default 3)'),
(44007, 1, 8, 255, 'In these days the bronze flight receives mortal visitors. At the threshold the Steward of Time greets travelers as if he had expected them, warns of the dangers that lie beyond his hall, and sends them down to the Keepers of Time in the depths. Below, tunnels called timeways lead into moments of history that strange beings are trying to unmake.', 'npc_text 9977, 9978 (Steward of Time); quest 10279 description; creature_text 19932 (beings tampering with the timeways); broadcast_text 17661 (timeways); mod-individual-progression ipp_aware_npcs.sql: Keepers of Time NPCs (20130, 19934, 19936, 19950, 19951, 20080-20082, 21643) are npc_ipp_tbc, visible from state 8; the Steward 20142 is not phased, so tagged by patch (2.0.3)'),
(44010, 1, 0, 255, 'The trolls are not the pool''s only danger. A junior surveyor who came to sample it was set upon at the water''s edge by something that crawled, and the attack forced the Water Company to admit that the stories of strange bugs drinking the desert dry were no nomad trick. For Gadgetzan it was the first warning of the silithid.', 'quest 992 reward text (ambushed by a creepy-crawly; reports of bugs sucking up the water)'),
(44016, 1, 0, 255, 'Scrimshank never came home. All that was carried back out of the chasm was his surveying gear, and the Water Company now counts him among its dead, hoping that what his instruments recorded before the end will make the loss mean something.', 'quest 10 description and reward text'),
(44020, 1, 0, 255, 'Fizzledowser owns that he should have warned his recruits. Reports of strange bugs drinking up the desert''s water had been coming in for some time, and he had waved them off as one more nomad trick, until his own surveyor was ambushed at Sandsorrow Watch. Now at least, he says, the company knows.', 'quest 992 reward text'),
(44020, 2, 0, 255, 'Then he lost Scrimshank. His top assistant never returned from the Gaping Chasm, and Fizzledowser, mourning a good goblin, pinned his hopes on whatever the recovered survey gear had recorded. The company''s research, he now believes, points to the bugs being steered by a third party, which bodes ill for the whole desert.', 'quest 10 description and reward text'),
(44020, 3, 0, 255, 'Fizzledowser is not thrilled about handing out the company''s valuable information for nothing, but he has known Pestlezugg for years. When the alchemist urged that everyone be warned of the bugs, he copied the report for all to read.', 'quest 113 description and reward text'),
(44022, 1, 0, 255, 'One taste of the gland''s water was enough to make Marin gag, yet he refused to give up. He passed the dew to Sprinkle, his friend and a fine cook, who calls him a good guy if a little eccentric and sighed that of course he needed her help yet again.', 'quest 2606 description and reward text'),
(44022, 2, 0, 255, 'Her secret mushroom powder transformed the brew. The result was the Noggenfogger Elixir, which Marin now sells and expects to make millions on. Sprinkle insists that he owes her one for it. Marin laughs that off as one of her jokes.', 'quests 2661, 2662 descriptions and reward texts; npc_vendor 7564 (Noggenfogger Elixir 8529)'),
(44024, 1, 0, 255, 'With the stone in hand, his memories came back. The room had six balconies, each with a serpent statue at its edge. Pushing one sprang a trap that nearly killed him, and from the ledge he glimpsed an altar to Hakkar below. He believes the circle of statues holds the secret to an even greater treasure.', 'quest 3444 reward text; quests 3446, 3447 descriptions'),
(44025, 1, 0, 255, 'Once the essence was in his hands, Yeh''kinya named the god: Hakkar the Soulflayer, whose return the trolls foretell, some as a coming glory for their race, others as the end of all things. The myth itself he professes to doubt. What he wants, he says, is to keep the power in Hakkar''s essence out of the hands of any who would misuse it.', 'quest 3520 reward text'),
(44025, 2, 0, 255, 'His tale sent helpers across the world, to Zul''Farrak for the tablets of Mosh''aru, to Jintha''Alor for an ancient egg and into the Sunken Temple for the essence of Hakkar''s avatar. When the filled egg came back to him and stirred, Yeh''kinya mused that the myths might be true after all, and he kept it, vowing that no evil hand would ever touch it.', 'quests 3527, 4787 descriptions; quest 3528 reward text'),
(44025, 3, 0, 255, 'The truth was darker. Yeh''kinya had served Hakkar all along. When his helpers came back to demand the egg, he cursed the meddling prospector Ironboot and declared it too late to save the world: the Soulflayer was already reborn in Zul''Gurub and growing in power, and with mock gratitude he told them their help had sped his return.', 'quest 8181 reward text; creature_text 8579'),
(44026, 1, 0, 255, 'Ironboot''s studies had shown him what the troll left out. The prophecy Yeh''kinya relied on rested on two tablets of Mosh''aru, but the dwarf knows of six, and he dreads what the missing four will say. Two of them, he has learned, lie with the Mossflayer trolls in the Eastern Plaguelands.', 'quest 5065 description'),
(44026, 2, 0, 255, 'His delvings into the tablets bore grim news. The egg was a cradle, not a prison: through it Hakkar himself could be born again. Ironboot sent the troll''s helpers back to Yeh''kinya to demand it, praying it was not too late.', 'quest 4788 reward text; quest 8181 description'),
(44026, 3, 0, 255, 'It was too late. Ironboot now puts his faith in the Zandalari, whose envoys have camped on Yojamba Isle near Stranglethorn, and sends heroes to their leader Molthor, hoping these trolls know a way to stop Hakkar before his new reign can spread across Azeroth.', 'quest 8182 description'),
(44027, 1, 0, 255, 'Behind the bluster he is a gifted engineer. When the blue dragon Azuregos needed an arcanite buoy built, he sent his plans to Narain, calling him a terrible, terrible psychic but an amazing engineer. Narain grumbled that the old goat knows he cannot read a word of Draconic.', 'npc_text 7897 (Azuregos); quest 8575 reward text, 8576 reward text'),
(44027, 2, 0, 255, 'Another grudge is older. His ex-best friend forever, Stewvul, stole his scrying goggles long ago, broke his heart in five places and left him here to rot, or so Narain tells it, and his crystal ball places the thief either at the Greymane Wall of Silverpine or somewhere far stranger.', 'quest 8577 description'),
(44027, 3, 0, 255, 'Doctor Weavil has struck at him through his most precious book. The only known copy of volume two of Draconic for Dummies, which Narain had hidden on an island far to the south, was booknapped, then torn into eight pieces and scattered to the wind, and Narain lays the blame squarely at his arch-enemy''s feet.', 'quests 8597, 8598 descriptions; quest 8620 description'),
(44027, 4, 0, 255, 'A mermaid loves him. Meridith of Land''s End Beach, who pulled him from the wreck of his flying machine, has sent word of her feelings. Narain fidgets at the very idea. She is a fish, he protests, and he is a gnome. It could never work out.', 'quest 8599 description and reward text'),
(44030, 1, 0, 255, 'The surveyor came back with tales of an ambush by some crawling horror. Fizzledowser confessed he had heard reports of bug-creatures sucking up the desert''s water and dismissed them as nomad shenanigans. Now he wanted to know the enemy, and sent for parts from the Centipaar of the Noxious Lair, where water pools once lay, for the alchemist Pestlezugg to examine.', 'quest 992 reward text; quest 82 description'),
(44030, 2, 0, 255, 'Pestlezugg found the parts unlike any insect he had ever seen, almost as if the bugs were controlled by an outside force. And there was an emergency. Fizzledowser''s top assistant, Scrimshank, had gone missing in the Gaping Chasm southeast of town, and the last word from him told of more of the same bugs.', 'quest 82 reward text; quest 10 description'),
(44030, 3, 0, 255, 'Only Scrimshank''s surveying gear came back from the chasm. Fizzledowser mourned a good goblin and hoped his death had not been in vain, for the research so far suggested that the bugs, too cunning for their own good, might be under the influence of a third party.', 'quest 10 reward text'),
(44030, 4, 0, 255, 'Pestlezugg''s analysis confirmed it. The bugs are controlled by a powerful and malignant force and have been changed into pure ravagers. The alchemist warned that they threaten not only Gadgetzan but all of southern Kalimdor, perhaps the whole of Azeroth, and urged that everyone be told.', 'quest 110 reward text; quest 113 description'),
(44030, 5, 0, 255, 'Fizzledowser, never thrilled to give company information away, made copies at his old friend''s urging, and the report went out to scholars in Orgrimmar and Darnassus who have studied the creatures of Azeroth, in the hope that they could say what the threat is and how it might be stopped.', 'quest 113 reward text; quests 32, 162 descriptions'),
(44031, 1, 0, 255, 'The bandits and thieves fell in enough numbers that the company could begin to plan how to win back its wells, but Bilgewhizzle was far from done. Next came the stronger ranks east and southeast of town, the rogues, assassins and shadow mages who guard the stolen wells, a nasty lot by his own account.', 'quest 1690 reward text; quest 1691 description'),
(44031, 2, 0, 255, 'With those ranks thinned as well, the nomads were few enough that the Gadgetzan Water Company could finally take the fight to them, and Bilgewhizzle began to speak of taking back what was rightfully the company''s.', 'quest 1691 description and reward text'),
(44031, 3, 0, 255, 'Caliph Scorpidsting''s head was brought to Bilgewhizzle, who declared that justice was served and paid the bounty in the company''s name. With the caliph dead, he hopes, the squatters may at last be pushed off Gadgetzan''s wells.', 'quest 2781 reward text'),
(44032, 1, 0, 255, 'The gland''s water tasted dreadful. Rather than give up, Marin had a brilliant idea: send the dew to his friend Sprinkle, an excellent cook, and have her make it go down easier. If it was going to taste that bad, he reasoned, it should at least have some kick.', 'quest 2605 reward text; quest 2606 description'),
(44032, 2, 0, 255, 'Sprinkle knew just the thing. As a child she had survived her sister''s horrible cooking with a secret ingredient, a mushroom called the Violet Tragan, which grows only underwater in a small lake of the Hinterlands. Add it to anything, she promised, and it tastes great.', 'quest 2641 description'),
(44032, 3, 0, 255, 'Ground into a violet powder and mixed with the dew, the mushroom produced the Noggenfogger Elixir. Marin, delighted, now plans to make millions on it and shoos his helpers aside so they do not block his business. Sprinkle reminds him he owes her a favor. Marin calls her such a kidder.', 'quests 2661, 2662 descriptions and reward texts; creature_text 7564 (mixing the elixir)'),
(44033, 1, 0, 255, 'Andre Firebeard''s head reached Bilgewhizzle at last. So the pirate would make his trial after all, the security chief remarked, and he paid for services rendered, assuring the one who brought it that the small print on the contract was quite harmless.', 'quest 2875 reward text'),
(44033, 2, 0, 255, 'One of the pirates was carrying the schedules of shipments between the port and Booty Bay, past and future, with ships marked for great loot or a hard fight. Bilgewhizzle was disturbed: with such a list, he said, a pirate captain could have himself a field day.', 'quest 2876 description and reward text'),
(44033, 3, 0, 255, 'The hats went to the Haughty Modiste, who means to have them cleaned and personalized and expects them to make her quite a bit of money, though she suggested that whoever fetched them spend some of the reward on a bath.', 'quest 8365 reward text'),
(44034, 1, 0, 255, 'The old god is Hakkar the Soulflayer, and the trolls have a prophecy that he will one day return. Yeh''kinya claimed not to believe it, only to want the god''s power kept from those who would abuse it. The prophecy of Mosh''aru, he said, told how to contain Hakkar''s essence. Its two tablets lay in Zul''Farrak, one with the long-dead martyr Theka, one with the hydromancer Velratha.', 'quest 3520 reward text; quest 3527 description'),
(44034, 2, 0, 255, 'Fused together, the tablets spoke of an ancient egg, a relic of the days when trolls ruled vast empires, with the power to hold the essence of Hakkar. It lay hidden in a cave behind the amphitheater atop Jintha''Alor in the Hinterlands, and Yeh''kinya wanted it brought to him.', 'quest 3527 reward text; quest 4787 description'),
(44034, 3, 0, 255, 'Carried into the Sanctum of the Fallen God within the Sunken Temple, the egg stirred the dead god. His avatar came forth and was slain, and its essence was drawn into the egg. When the filled egg stirred with life, Yeh''kinya wondered whether the myths were true, and took it into his keeping, promising to keep it from evil hands.', 'quest 3528 description and reward text'),
(44035, 1, 0, 255, 'The fifth and sixth tablets were held by the Smolderthorn trolls within Blackrock Spire, a dark mountain of fire between the Burning Steppes and the Searing Gorge, and Ironboot sent his helpers there while he pored over the third and fourth.', 'quest 5065 reward text; quest 4788 description'),
(44035, 2, 0, 255, 'Reading the tablets together, Ironboot found the hidden half of the legend. The egg was never meant to contain the Soulflayer. Hakkar''s true form could be born again through the very egg into which his essence had been captured. Yeh''kinya had led his helpers astray, and they were sent back to demand the egg from him.', 'quest 8181 description'),
(44035, 3, 0, 255, 'Confronted, Yeh''kinya only gloated that it was too late. Hakkar was reborn in the ancient troll city of Zul''Gurub and grew in power there, and the troll thanked his dupes for hastening the Soulflayer''s return.', 'quest 8181 reward text; creature_text 8579'),
(44035, 4, 0, 255, 'Ironboot''s worst fears had come. Legend spoke of the Soulflayer ruling the ancient troll world through terror, and he feared the new reign could spread across Azeroth. He sent the troll''s former helpers to Molthor of the Zandalari on Yojamba Isle, off the coast of Stranglethorn, whose trolls might know how to defeat the blood god.', 'quest 8182 description'),
(44036, 1, 0, 255, 'The goggles had been stolen long ago by Stewvul, once Narain''s best friend forever, who turned up hiding in a crate beside the Greymane Wall in Silverpine. He was glad to give them back, except that he had lost them a month before while nosing around in the Molten Core.', 'quest 8577 description; quest 8578 description; DB: crate 180642 at the Greymane Wall (area 230)'),
(44036, 2, 0, 255, 'Dirge swore there was no such thing as a five hundred pound chicken, not anymore. Instead he had the carcass of the chimaerok lord, Lord Lakmaeran of the Isle of Dread in Feralas, brought to him, and with rocket fuel, deeprock salt and his own spices he made his greatest creation, Dirge''s Kickin'' Chimaerok Chops.', 'quests 8584, 8585 descriptions and reward texts; quest 8586 description and reward text'),
(44036, 3, 0, 255, 'The book had been booknapped, a ransom note left in its place. A decoy drop in Winterspring failed, and the culprit proved to be Narain''s arch-enemy, Doctor Weavil, who tore the only known copy into eight parts and scattered them to the wind. They had to be found and bound back together.', 'quests 8597, 8598, 8606 reward texts; quest 8620 description'),
(44036, 4, 0, 255, 'At last Narain read the ledger and, given a great deal of arcanite, elementium ore and rare gems, built the buoy. Only then did he mention the bad news: Maws, a hundred feet of death and destruction, waits where the buoy is meant to be cast, in the Bay of Storms off Azshara.', 'quest 8728 description and reward text; quest 8729 description (offered at the 8728 turn-in)'),
(44037, 1, 0, 255, 'Andormu sent a custodian to guide newcomers through the cavern. The keepers, she explained, watch over Nozdormu''s realm and mend its ordinary disturbances, such as a rogue mage changing the past to raise his station. The master never meddles in mortal affairs and only corrects what others alter, yet he is away now, which means someone is trying to change time on a grand scale.', 'quest 10277 description; broadcast_text 17656, 17659, 17660 (Custodian of Time)'),
(44037, 2, 0, 255, 'The tunnels around them are timeways, infinite in number. Those open now are trouble spots born of a single disturbance, ranked from least to most catastrophic, though the collapse of any one would end the world. At one she named the culprits, a malevolent organization called the Infinite Dragonflight. There are only two truths here, she said: time is always in flux, and perception does not dictate reality.', 'broadcast_text 17661, 17662, 17663, 17667 (Custodian of Time); quest 10277 reward text');
